+### A text into an int8
+
+`lv_i8 = lv_text.` lowers to `abap.ParseI8` (go/abap conv.go, js/abap.mjs):
+ParseI's rule for the wider range -- the same texts are numbers (`12-` is -12,
+blanks around the sign are part of the text, an empty text is 0, `1E3` and
+`12 3` are no number), the fraction rounds half away from zero, and the
+overflow is only past int8's range, so `3000000000` fits where it overflows an
+i and `9223372036854775807.5` does not fit once the rounding has done its
+work. Both int8 endpoints are kept exactly: Go takes the magnitude into a
+uint64 and the negative endpoint from the magnitude one out of int64 rather
+than negating it in int64, JS holds a BigInt. The raised class is what a
+`CATCH cx_sy_conversion_overflow` / `cx_sy_conversion_no_number` matches on
+(Go an `ArithmeticError`, JS an `AbapError`), so the fixture catches both.
